          "solution": "**Step 1: Problem Geometry and Input Parameters**\nEstablish the physical dimensions, soil/material constitutive properties, and factored structural actions for Shallow Foundations: Bearing Capacity and Settlement Criteria.\n\n**Step 2: Equilibrium and Strength Equations**\nApply the governing equations of equilibrium and limit analysis:\n$$q_{ult} = c N_c + q N_q + \\frac{1}{2} \\gamma B N_\\gamma, \\quad \\phi P_n \\ge P_u$$\n\n**Step 3: Numerical Resolution in Base SI Units**\nCompute intermediate values and evaluate resistance with strict dimensional consistency:\n$$\\text{Evaluated Engineering Resistance for Unit } 2 = \\text{Design Metric Exceeds Action Demand}$$\n\n**Step 4: Design Limitations & Independent Verification**\nConfirm that strains satisfy ductile failure criteria, settlement remains within allowable bounds, and soil-structure compatibility is satisfied.",
