          "content": "## Unit 3 synthesis\n\nThis unit connects its four lessons through one overarching design decision: the right model follows from the mechanism and evidence, not from a convenient formula. Prepare a one-page design-basis table listing assumptions, parameter origin, uncertainty, sensitivity, and the condition requiring professional escalation. Pair that table with a labeled cross-section. For the investigation or structure in your own scenario, justify whether the controlling concern is ultimate resistance, unacceptable movement, unexpected groundwater, temporary construction loading or interaction with neighbors. Do not confuse a numerical check with an approval; identify the external standard and reviewer required for a real project.\n\n**Paired simulations:** [Lab 05](../labs/lab-05.html) and [Lab 06](../labs/lab-06.html).\n\n**Assessment:** [Unit 03 questions](../assessments/unit-03.html).\n\n**Project:** Raft stiffness and localized soft zones \u2014 Model a 20 m \u00d7 12 m raft with three columns and a soft patch near one corner. Provide overall force and moment balance, spring sensitivity, a sketch of predicted settlement profiles and a monitoring concept. Explain why the toy load-spreading simulation is not a validated plate solution."
